===Conservation licence plates===
In 2013, the province introduced five new specialty plate designs. Those designs included; Blue jay, Canada goose, Red fox, Trout & Lady slipper, the provinces official flower. All profits go to the P.E.I. Wildlife Conservation Fund.<ref>{{cite web|title=New Licence Plate|url=http://www.gov.pe.ca/highwaysafety/index.php3?number=1047720&lang=E|website=www.gov.pe.ca/highwaysafety|publisher=Highway Safety Division|access-date=12 September 2014|date=2013-10-03}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=5 conservation licence plates offered by P.E.I. |url=https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/prince-edward-island/5-conservation-licence-plates-offered-by-p-e-i-1.1872951 |website=CBC News |access-date=19 September 2022}}</ref>
